#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096449 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096650 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b8b30414-400e-5c93-98d4-82299b4eb570" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Linear Combination of Two Vectors"}] :question/id #uuid "2ff4e8a9-d5ef-5e00-bba9-b51e18bf1f24" :question/math-academy-id "e-4284" :question/problem "Given the vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ shown below, draw the linear combination $2\\mathbf{a}+3\\mathbf{b}$.\n\n![](images/32/325e4a450d89ee1f5db4afd237dbc7d58efafec72d080386788f0491cc35950b.png)" :question/worked-solution "- The vector $2\\mathbf{a}$ has the same direction as $\\mathbf{a}$ but twice the magnitude.\n- Likewise, the vector $3\\mathbf{b}$ has the same direction as $\\mathbf{b}$ but three times the magnitude.\n\n![](images/06/066784522a39671fe57b157c6c692f5c56295126b8ec6f150d917e783ab63400.png)\n\nNow, we can draw $3\\mathbf{b}$ starting from the head of $2\\mathbf{a}$. The resultant\n$2\\mathbf{a}+3\\mathbf{b}$\ngoes from the tail of $2\\mathbf{a}$ to the head of $3\\mathbf{b}$.\n\n![](images/d1/d1dd084ad4f8f717afac515471bcba679fbe545f266435a57fb1c94d0d5c9cca.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096450 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096651 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2121109d-7b73-5609-a9df-1eeed257ab1b" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Statement With Linear Combinations Whose Coefficients Are Linear Functions"}] :question/id #uuid "f8325830-9c74-5bf2-866c-1c31acdcc37c" :question/math-academy-id "e-4285" :question/problem "Suppose we are given two vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ where $\\mathbf{a} \\nparallel \\mathbf{b}$. Find $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$, if\n\n$\\mathbf{a}+7\\mathbf{b}=(2\\alpha+\\beta)\\mathbf{a}-\\beta\\mathbf{b}$." :question/worked-solution "Since $\\mathbf{a} \\nparallel \\mathbf{b}$, the linear combination can only be written in one way. So, the coefficients of $\\mathbf{a}$ must be equal, and the coefficients of $\\mathbf{b}$ must be equal.\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get:\n\n$$\n{1 = 2α + β; 7 = - β\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nβ &= -7\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting back into the first equation, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n1 &= 2α + β \\\\\n1 &= 2α + (-7) \\\\\n8 &= 2α \\\\\nα &= 4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that $\\alpha = 4$ and $\\beta = -7$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096970 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096651 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2121109d-7b73-5609-a9df-1eeed257ab1b" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Statement With Linear Combinations Whose Coefficients Are Linear Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "815379c2-1a2e-502f-88e9-fc031e15b9ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$s = 3$ and $t =-4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093795} {:answer/id #uuid "a1f896da-f25a-53e4-ac3c-bf271b59ffd6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$s = 3$ and $t =-1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093796} {:answer/id #uuid "c5a93eff-2597-5f20-9e9a-88546a01c848" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$s = 3$ and $t = 1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093797} {:answer/id #uuid "48a4eb85-e4e4-5fca-9c6d-be8aa3f29fe8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$s =-3$ and $t =-1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093798} {:answer/id #uuid "7346fe82-3d08-5a9e-a3ad-7377097cd7b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$s = 2$ and $t =-2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093799}] :answer-field/id #uuid "d0aa4fe7-2cc8-577f-85fb-d7c9d634e92d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093794}] :question/id #uuid "e29e9257-b1b8-5da4-a181-19b32ffa49a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-11381" :question/problem "Suppose we are given two vectors $a$ and $b$ where $a∦b$. Find $s$ and $t$, if\n$5a + 4b = (2s + t)a + (s - t)b$."}]}
